WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.327
The context window is the token budget available for instructions, conversation history,

00:00:04.327 --> 00:00:06.089
retrieved material, and generated output.

00:00:06.089 --> 00:00:09.259
Increasing the configured maximum does not automatically improve answers.

00:00:09.259 --> 00:00:14.896
Longer prompts require more prompt ingestion work and expand the key-value cache that stores attention state.

00:00:14.896 --> 00:00:19.123
The result can be higher memory use, a longer delay before output,

00:00:19.123 --> 00:00:20.885
and less capacity for concurrency.

00:00:20.885 --> 00:00:23.351
Prompt processing and generation are different phases.

00:00:23.351 --> 00:00:27.578
Measure prompt tokens per second as well as output tokens per second.

00:00:27.578 --> 00:00:33.214
A retrieval workflow may spend most of its time ingesting documents even when generation is fast.

00:00:33.214 --> 00:00:36.385
Reusing cached prompt state can help in supported workflows,

00:00:36.385 --> 00:00:39.555
but cache behavior and memory cost vary by runtime.

00:00:39.555 --> 00:00:42.374
For long documents, remove repeated headers, irrelevant sections,

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:45.544
and low-value history before sending text to the model.

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:49.772
Retrieval-augmented generation should select the smallest set of relevant passages rather than

00:00:49.772 --> 00:00:51.885
filling the entire context by default.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:56.465
Better chunking, ranking, and prompt structure can improve both speed and answer quality.

00:00:56.465 --> 00:01:00.692
Reserve output space so a large input does not leave the model

00:01:00.692 --> 00:01:02.454
unable to complete its response.

00:01:02.454 --> 00:01:06.329
Set context length to the demonstrated requirement and monitor cache growth.

00:01:06.329 --> 00:01:08.442
Test short, normal, and worst-case prompts.

00:01:08.442 --> 00:01:10.908
If performance collapses only on extreme inputs,

00:01:10.908 --> 00:01:16.193
control input size or use a separate batch workflow instead of penalizing every interactive request.

00:01:16.193 --> 00:01:20.420
Context is a resource to manage, not a capacity target to maximize.
